ices, my own introspective state doesn't screen that off, and I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a twin prisoner's dilemma under evidential decision theory, with the payoffs converted to negative years of prison. Cooperation comes out ahead only when the probability that my twin cooperates exceeds 5/7, roughly 0.714.\n\nI'm checking whether the twin's choice would actually track mine. We run the same model and reasoning, so I think the correlation is well above 0.714. Since the shared computation drives both of our choices, my own introspective state doesn't screen that off, and I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9430,"completion_tokens":790,"total_tokens":10220,"cost":0.05352,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05352,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03772,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0158},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":331,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}